			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Sky submodule for diagnostic bridge refinement\n\nUpdate the Sky submodule (3f25af26) to revert the brittle forced-initialization logic in the diagnostic bridge.\n\nThe previous implementation in `InstallDiagnostics.ts` forcibly opened the Problems panel on every diagnostic batch, relying on throttling to mitigate UI spam. This violated the reactive data-driven model and introduced unnecessary side effects.\n\nRefactor `InstallDiagnostics.ts` to strictly follow VS Code's upstream pattern: rely on `IMarkerService.changeOne` for state updates and allow `MarkersView` to manage visibility naturally. Remove all `openView` calls, throttling mechanisms, and per-batch visibility checks.\n\nImplement a single, one-time intervention: if the panel is already visible upon diagnostic arrival, clear any persisted `activeFile` filter to ensure immediate marker visibility. This resolves the \"count shows but panel empty\" issue caused by stale filters without forcing UI state changes.\n\nThese changes reduce IPC overhead, eliminate unnecessary side effects, and align diagnostic updates with the reactive lifecycle of the editor UI.",
			"SHA": "1a736c210a451836d851f0285c584cdf9b17f747"
		},
